{#
  What a post reposts, likes or bookmarks (TASK-169), cited the way a reply
  cites what it answers: each one an embedded `h-cite` under its own mf2
  property, `u-repost-of`, `u-like-of` or `u-bookmark-of`, that always carries
  the target's URL, so a parser reads what the post cites and the page its
  webmention names links to it.

  Drawn as the same citation block as `reply-context.njk` (doc-9). An entry
  includes it with `citations` on the context, a list of `{ property, url,
  context }`; a feed sets it from the entry it is printing.

  `context` is what the target said about itself when the post was saved or
  synced (TASK-244), only when it said something: its `name` and `author`,
  printed through autoescaping like a reply's context. With a name, the name
  is the link; with only an author, "a post" is; for a URL that is an image,
  "an image from" its host; with nothing, "a page on" its host.

  `context.picture` is the target's picture, copied into the site's uploads
  (TASK-252), absent when there is none or the post hid its previews. A
  repost of a photo (`picture.full`) shows it in full under the line; any
  other citation shows it as a thumbnail beside the line. Both link to the
  target, and `picture.html` is the `img.u-photo` inside the `h-cite`.
#}
{% import "partials/cited-page.njk" as cited %}
{% set citationVerbs = { "repost-of": "Reposted", "like-of": "Liked", "bookmark-of": "Bookmarked" } %}
{% for citation in citations %}
{% set citedPage = citation.context %}
{% set picture = citedPage.picture %}
<div class="reply-context cite u-{{ citation.property }} h-cite{% if picture and not picture.full %} cite-with-thumb{% endif %}">
  {%- if picture and not picture.full %}{{ cited.thumb(citation.url, picture) }}{% endif %}
  <p class="cite-line small">{{ citationVerbs[citation.property] }}
    {{- cited.page(citation.url, citedPage) -}}
  </p>
  {%- if picture.full %}
  <a class="cite-photo" href="{{ citation.url }}">{{ picture.html | safe }}</a>
  {%- endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
